SDUSD::deposit
├── given PAUSE_TYPE is paused
│   └── it should revert with IsPaused
└── given PAUSE_TYPE is not paused
    ├── when receiver is zero address
    │   └── it should revert with ERC20InvalidReceiver
    ├── when caller has insufficient DUSD balance or allowance
    │   ├── it should revert with the underlying token transfer error
    │   └── it should leave accounted assets, deposit cap usage, and share supply unchanged
    ├── when assets exceeds maxDeposit for receiver
    │   ├── it should revert with ERC4626ExceededMaxDeposit
    │   └── it should leave deposit cap usage and vault state unchanged
    ├── when total supply is zero
    │   ├── it should transfer assets from caller to the vault
    │   ├── it should increase accountedAssets by assets
    │   ├── it should exclude only the exact initial seed deposit to address(1) from principal
    │   ├── it should mint all previewed shares to receiver
    │   ├── it should count ordinary first deposits toward the receiver principal and depositCapUsage
    │   ├── it should return the full previewed share amount
    │   ├── it should emit Deposit
    │   └── it should not decrease the initial exchange rate
    └── when total supply is non-zero
        ├── it should transfer assets from caller to the vault
        ├── it should increase accountedAssets by assets
        ├── it should increase the receiver principal and depositCapUsage by the deposited assets
        ├── it should mint the previewed shares to receiver
        ├── it should leave the seed share balance unchanged
        ├── it should return the previewed share amount
        ├── it should emit Deposit
        ├── it should not decrease the exchange rate because shares round down in favor of the vault
        ├── when assets is zero
        │   ├── it should complete without changing accounting or balances
        │   ├── it should leave depositCapUsage unchanged
        │   ├── it should emit Deposit with zero assets and shares
        │   └── it should preserve the exchange rate
        ├── when assets is non-zero and the share amount rounds down to zero
        │   ├── it should revert with SDUSDZeroShares
        │   └── it should leave asset balances, accountedAssets, and share balances unchanged
        ├── when a reward period is active
        │   ├── it should price the deposit using only currently unlocked assets
        │   ├── rewards should not change depositCapUsage and the deposit should add only its assets
        │   └── it should not decrease the exchange rate when shares round down
        ├── when assets equals the remaining cap headroom
        │   ├── it should accept the deposit
        │   └── it should consume all remaining headroom
        └── when the vault has received a raw DUSD donation
            ├── it should ignore the donation when calculating shares
            ├── it should leave the exchange rate unchanged before the deposit
            └── it should not decrease the exchange rate when the deposit rounds shares down
